  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Assistance of Venezuelan Migrants Victims of Trafficking</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention aims to improve the regional prevention capacities and protection services for Venezuelan victims of trafficking and for those at risk of becoming victims. The initiative will rely on IOM&apos;s existing operational capacity in the region to support awareness raising among communities and service providers and improve coordination and referral mechanisms.  To achieve this, the project will focus on strengthening skills and knowledge of relevant stakeholders and institutions in the region to provide a counter trafficking response, through the development and validation of a regional toolkit for the early identification of potential victims of trafficking.</narrative>
  </description>
